00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Subs: English

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
S

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
<b><i>SILVER ZERO
 SUBS</i></b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
http://silverzerosubs.blogspot.com/

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.600
Grandfather's Mountain Cabin

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.750
<i>The orphan Heidi, who has been brought
up by her aunt Dete until she is five,</i>

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:38.420
<i>is to be left in the care of her grandfather,
who lives in a mountain cabin in the alps.</i>

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.970
<i>But what awaits her when
she finally arrives is,</i>

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.600
<i>true to the rumors in the village,</i>

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.350
<i>the truly unsociable and stern
countenance of her grandfather.</i>

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:58.680
If you don't want to take the responsibility,
you can do what you like.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:00.520
Whatever happens will be your fault!

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.270
So you...
- Go away!

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.750
I've heard enough.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.930
Be off with you this instant, you hear me?

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.580
{++++MJN And do not let me see
your face again in a hurry.}Don't show yourself here again, got it?

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:17.960
Come here Heidi.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:20.890
Take care of yourself.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.550
Goodbye, Aunt.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.360
Dete!

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.000
Dete.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.760
{++++MJN You really left her on Alm-Uncle's hut?}You really left her at the old man's place?

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:52.520
Yes.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.070
How could you? Poor child.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.200
I didn't have a choice.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.140
That's right.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.360
{++++MJN Did you think I could take
such a small child with me?}Are you saying I should take
a child that's just turned five

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.020
{++++MJN}along with me to work?

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.320
I couldn't.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.640
{++++MJN I've found a good job}You know, I finally found
a good job opening,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.080
{++++MJN in a nice family's house, where
they'll pay me well.}with good pay,
and I want to be free to take it.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.640
{++++MJNI'm sorry about her, but...}The people around me
can say whatever they want,

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.530
{++++MJN I have to think about myself.}but it's not like I'm happy about it.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:26.870
Do you understand, Miss Barbel?
You understand me right?

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:28.890
But...

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.440
{++++MJN I don't have a choice, I really don't.}It can't be helped! I didn't have
any choice but to do it.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.520
Dete!

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.040
Dete!

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.280
Well, what do you plan to do from now on?

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.550
I want to see what you
have inside the house.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.140
Come then!

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.810
{++++MJN Bring that!}Bring your bundle of clothes in with you.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.220
{++++MJN I shan't want them any more.}I don't need it anymore.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.890
{++++MJN You certainly are not very smart.}You're a strange child, aren't you.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.280
{++++MJN And why don't you want them any more?}Why don't you need it anymore?

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.650
{++++MJN Because I want to go about like the goats.}I want to run around like a goat!

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.710
{++++MJN Bring your bundle of clothes in with you.}Yes, but bring your clothes.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:26.810
{++++in}Do I put them in here?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.290
{++++MJN Yes. Down there.}Yes. Then close the closet.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.510
What a big pot!

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.330
It smells like cheese.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:42.870
Yes, it does.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.530
It's you who makes the
cheese, Grandfather?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:52.430
I want to learn how to make cheese, too.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.990
Where am I to sleep?

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.520
Wherever you like.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.400
Where should I sleep?

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:24.450
{++++MJN So much hay!}Lots of hay!

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.940
{++++MJN Smells good.}It smells good!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.250
Ah! It's so beautiful!

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:48.830
Ah!

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.130
What's wrong?

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.910
{++++MJN You, what's wrong?}What? What's going on?

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:12.900
Smells good.
Grandfather, I really like this smell.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.040
I shall sleep up here.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:20.760
I'll sleep on this soft hay!

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.270
Now, I have to make a bed!

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.730
Grandfather, can you bring me some sheets?

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:31.520
Beds are things you spread
sheets over and sleep on.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:34.050
Come on, hurry up.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.890
A-all right.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.420
This girl is smart.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:45.890
Hurry up!

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:46.970
All right.

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:52.130
What do you think?

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.000
Good work.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.790
Isn't it? In this bed I can
see the mountains and the trees.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:00.810
Look!

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.450
Wait just a bit.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.660
What do you think, Heidi?

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:22.660
Fluffy, fluffy.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.040
Now the sheet.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.840
It's a fine bed.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:39.250
But we have forgotten something now.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:44.460
A coverlid. When you get into bed, you
need something to cover you. Don't you?

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.970
You're right. But suppose I don't have one.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.330
Well, never mind.
I can take some more hay to put over me.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.160
Wait a moment.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:02.370
Oh, what a big sack.
Will I sleep inside of it?

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:04.010
I wonder if I'll fit...

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:06.180
Well then...

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:15.640
Well, what do you think?

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:17.310
Great, great!

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.950
{++++MJN That is a splendid coverlid.}That's a really splendid blanket!

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:24.100
{++++MJN Don't you think it looks like a King's bed?}With this we can even let a king stay here!

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:25.200
That's right.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.700
Like a King's bed.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:31.110
Yes. It is a bed fit for a king.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:36.310
And this poor cabin is our castle.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.650
From here we can see the beautiful
stars in the sky, at night.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:43.660
That's right.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:48.330
{++++MJN Grandfather, maybe I can hear
the birds singing in the morning.}Grandfather, I wonder if the birds come to
say "Good morning!" in the morning.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.440
{++++MJN Yes, you'll hear them.}Of course, they come.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:55.790
{++++MJN}The wind might knock on the window
like a mischievous boy,

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.210
{++++MJN}but that's just a greeting
to the king of the castle.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:01.290
{++++MJN}When you get used to it, he can be
a pretty good person to talk to.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:06.630
{++++MJN}A rainy day brings sad things to think about.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:09.340
{++++MJN}Humans need that kind of day.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.300
I don't like the rain.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.760
I really don't!

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.860
Me neither.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.810
I wish it was night.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.110
{++++MJN So that I might get inside my bed at once.}Aaah, I want to try out the bed.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:41.370
{++++MJN I think we might have something to eat first.
What do you think?}More importantly, let's go downstairs and
have lunch. You must be hungry, right?

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.060
{++++MJN Yes, I think so too.}Yes, I'm really hungry!

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.750
{++++MJN We both think alike.}Seems like we agree.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:48.380
Well, let us go down then.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.890
<i>While just talking to Heidi,</i>

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:56.400
<i>even this grumpy old man
feels a strange sense...</i>

00:10:56.440 --> 00:11:01.150
<i>of becoming unusually joyful and cheerful,</i>

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:03.650
<i>and that his heart is calmed.</i>

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:29.450
Looks delicious!

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.330
I see that you have some ideas of your own.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.090
But there is still something missing.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.200
What could it be?

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.280
Here.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.210
Good.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.460
What will you do for a seat?

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:38.400
I am afraid it is rather low.

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:40.300
All right, let's do this.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.060
What a wonderful table.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.270
Here, eat.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.200
Thanks for the food!

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.690
Delicious.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:08.080
This is the first time I've had milk this delicious!

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:13.090
Really? Then you must have some more!
Goat milk is good for the body.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:13.640
Yes!

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:16.400
Huh?

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.800
Oh!

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:24.390
Koro...Koro...

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.620
Koro. Koro!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.710
It's Joseph.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.500
His name is Joseph?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:43.610
{++++MJN At Aunt Ursula's house,
there was a dog called Koro.}The dog at Grandma Ursel's
house was called Koro.

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:48.020
That must be where Dete
used to leave you, right?

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:49.750
Joseph.

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.270
But he's not cute.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:20.530
Come on, eat your food.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:21.420
Yes!

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.090
{++++MJN I'm going to play.}Thanks for the meal!

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:00.060
{++++MJN This dog just sleeps.}He's sleeping again.

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.360
I'm sorry!

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.540
Heidi!

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:05.860
What is it?

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.890
Go put your clothes on!
It's getting cold.

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:10.890
Yes.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:18.690
What are you doing, Grandfather?

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:20.990
What do you think it is?

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.450
Ah, it's a stool, right?

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.990
That's it! It's a stool for me!

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:34.910
It's so high!

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.030
{***Timing}Isn't it, Grandfather?

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.210
Well, it's done. Here.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.610
Thank you, Grandfather.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:55.360
It's my stool.
It's my stool.

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.870
She understands what she sees.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.770
Her eyes are in the right place.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:19.600
<i>Heidi completely forgets about
the small downtown room...</i>

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.810
<i>where she had been taken care
of until that morning.</i>

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:26.270
<i>Deeply breathing the delicious
air of the wide alp meadows,</i>

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:29.650
<i>Heidi's heart rejoices to the utmost.</i>

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.020
Are you going to bite me?

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:47.850
Are you?

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:55.100
I'm Heidi!

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.240
{++++MJN Now I live here.}I'll be living here from now on.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.440
Do you want to be my friend?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.330
Oh! Joseph, you...

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.910
Say something!

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.100
Woof!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.800
Woof woof!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:20.610
Woof!

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.780
Woof woof!

00:18:57.760 --> 00:18:59.040
Welcome!

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:08.760
Snowflake!

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.060
Welcome back, Snowflake.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.540
Are these our goats?

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.120
{++++MJN}Yes. They're Little Swan and Little Bear.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.530
{++++}I see.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.140
What's that?

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:34.340
It's salt. They love it.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.760
Let me give them salt.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:40.530
Here, eat it.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:45.560
It tickles!

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:51.010
Hey, Goat General!
Don't be late tomorrow!

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:54.860
{++++ MJN N-no... It won't happen again.
Well, goodbye.}I won't oversleep again. Goodbye!

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:59.720
Goodbye, Peter!

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.800
I'll see you tomorrow!

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:04.080
Goodbye!

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.160
Grandfather, what are we going to do now?

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:23.050
We're going to sleep.
But first we're going to eat.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:25.350
Sleep?

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:28.510
That's right.
It's still sunny because it's summer.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:31.940
Then, Little Swan, Little Bear,
good night.

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:42.990
Huh?

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:45.790
Aunt Ursula, I'm going to the mountains.

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:48.770
What? It's already noon?

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:50.880
No. I'm going to the mountains.

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:54.360
If you're going to play, play inside the house.

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:59.830
If something happens to you,
I won't get paid.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:01.530
No, that's not what I said!

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:02.620
What?

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:06.180
I'm going to my Grandfather's place!
To the Alm mountain!

00:22:24.010 --> 00:22:26.930
I wonder if the child will be frightened.

00:22:55.740 --> 00:23:01.060
Go ahead and close your eyes

00:22:55.740 --> 00:23:01.060
Itteoide me wo tojite

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:06.780
Into the dream, the way of the dream

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:06.780
Yume no naka he yume no michi he

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:11.800
Good night, cute goats

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:11.800
Kawaii yagi mo oyasumi

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.960
in the pen,

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.960
Koya no naka

00:23:15.650 --> 00:23:18.450
Good night, echoes

00:23:15.650 --> 00:23:18.450
Kodama mo oyasumi

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:22.900
in the valleys,

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:22.900
Tani no oku de

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:31.500
Good night! Good night!

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:31.500
Oyasumi oyasumi

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.840
<i>Outside, the wind is blowing violently.</i>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:41.060
<i>But Heidi is warm, and soundly
asleep, breathing quietly,</i>

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:45.550
<i>in the brand new hay bed
that she has made herself.</i>

00:23:55.620 --> 00:24:02.330
<i>The next morning, Peter takes Heidi along with
the goats to the mountain pastures.</i>

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:04.750
<i>The flowers that spread out everywhere,</i>

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:06.960
<i>the deep valleys with leftover snow,</i>

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:11.920
<i>and the rare animals of the alps,
all greatly delights Heidi.</i>

00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:15.340
<i>Eating lunch surrounded by the fresh air,</i>

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:18.260
<i>almost dropping down a cliff.</i>

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:20.680
<i>Nothing but fun!</i>

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:22.860
<i>Next time:
The Mountain Pasture</i>

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.230
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

